{"toolCallId":"call_2c27d52e768b4a25906da2181b569499","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"\nSpec Folder Validation v3.0.0\n\n  Folder: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n  Level:  3\n  Engine: orchestrator\n\n+ FILE_EXISTS: All required files present for Level 3\n! PLACEHOLDER_FILLED: 6 unfilled value token(s) in a Draft packet. Fill each one before the status leaves Draft\n    - implementation-summary.md:50: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Opening hook: 2-3 sentences on what changed and why it matters. Lead with impact.]\n    - implementation-summary.md:61: | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: path] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Created/Modified/Deleted] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What this change accomplishe\n    - implementation-summary.md:70: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How was this tested, verified and shipped? What was the rollout approach?]\n    - implementation-summary.md:81: | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What was decided] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Active-voice rationale with specific reasoning] |\n    - implementation-summary.md:92: | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Validation, lint, tests, manual check] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: PASS/FAIL with specifics] |\n    - implementation-summary.md:101: 1. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Limitation]** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Specific detail with workaround if one exists.]\n+ TEMPLATE_SOURCE: Template source headers present\n+ ANCHORS_VALID: Anchors well formed in 5 file(s)\n+ FRONTMATTER_VALID: Frontmatter continuity basics present\n+ FRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK: All spec-doc frontmatter memory blocks are structurally valid\n+ SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY: All targeted spec-doc anchors meet the sufficiency baseline\n+ MERGE_LEGALITY: No merge plan supplied; legality check skipped\n+ CROSS_ANCHOR_CONTAMINATION: No routing payload supplied; contamination check skipped\n+ POST_SAVE_FINGERPRINT: No post-save payload supplied; fingerprint check skipped\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_PRESENT: Graph metadata checked\nx GENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY: Generated metadata integrity found 1 violation(s) (enforced)\n    - graph-metadata.json: SOURCE_FINGERPRINT_MISMATCH: source_fingerprint does not match a re-derive of the current source docs, the stored derived fields may be stale\nx GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT: Generated metadata drift found 1 drifted field(s) (enforced)\n    - description: stored 'Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh' drifted from fresh '`recommend-level.sh` prints a human report: a blank line, the level line, the score line, a six-line breakdown, and a phase section that appears by'\n+ COMMENT_HYGIENE_MARKER: No ephemeral comment-hygiene markers found\n+ SCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED: Spec status is 'Draft', not Complete; scaffold markers are allowed\n+ STATUS_CROSS_DOC_CONSISTENCY: status cross-doc check not applicable; one status is missing or unclassified\n    - spec.md Status=Draft classified=planned\n    - implementation-summary.md Status=<missing> classified=unknown\n+ AC_COVERAGE: Acceptance coverage gate not active for this level or lifecycle state\n+ TOC_POLICY: TOC policy passed: no TOC headings in non-research spec documents\n+ AI_PROTOCOLS: AI protocols present and complete (4/4)\n+ COMPLEXITY_MATCH: Complexity level consistent with content (Level 3; phases=3, tasks=71, stories=2, scenarios=0)\n+ FOLDER_NAMING: Folder name '001-recommend-level-quiet-flag' follows naming convention\n+ FRONTMATTER_VALUES: Frontmatter values are in the shared list\n+ SOURCE_TAGS: No [SOURCE:] path:line citations in research or review artifacts\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"453ec0","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_2e394869221f48fc8a6dfb664dd27bbe","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"2:title: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\n3:description: \"Add a --quiet branch to one bash script: parse the flag, keep the JSON conflict explicit, and print only the Recommended Level line at dispatch. Prove it with a line count on both modes and a byte diff against a captured baseline.\"\n5:  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\n10:# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n29:The change lives in one file. `--quiet` joins the existing `case` parser as a boolean global, the parser rejects `--json --quiet` before any scoring runs, and the output dispatch gains a one-line branch that reuses the label `output_text` already prints. Verification compares line counts for the quiet and default forms and diffs the default output against a baseline captured before the edit.\n59:- **Argument parser** (section 5): reads `--quiet` into `QUIET` and rejects the `--json` conflict before scoring.\n60:- **Output dispatch** (section 7): sends text mode to `output_text` or to the one-line quiet branch; JSON mode is untouched.\n64:Arguments become globals, the score functions read those globals, `determine_level` sets the level and `calculate_confidence` sets the confidence. `--quiet` is read once in the parser and consulted only at dispatch, so no scoring function sees it and no arithmetic changes.\n77:| `output_text` | prints the 17-line report and the level label | unchanged | the quiet branch reuses the label at line 510 and leaves the function body alone |\n78:| Callers that read the default report | humans and any script that scrapes the report | not a consumer of `--quiet` | SC-002 diffs the default output against the captured baseline |\n79:| Callers that pass `--json` | read one JSON document | not a consumer of `--quiet` | AC-004 pins the rejection path |\n80:| `show_help` and the header OPTIONS block | document the option surface | update | `rg -n -- '--quiet' recommend-level.sh` finds the header, the parser, the help text and the branch |\n83:- Same-class producers: `rg -n 'JSON_OUTPUT|RECOMMEND_PHASES' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` lists every output-mode global; `QUIET` joins that set and follows the same shape.\n85:- Matrix axes: output mode (default, `--quiet`, `--json`, `--quiet --json`) crossed with input profile (low, medium, full-risk, invalid). AC-001 through AC-006 cover the quiet rows and the JSON conflict; T012 covers the invalid-input rows.\n86:- Algorithm invariant: not a path, redaction, parser-resolver or security fix; the only invariant is that stdout without `--quiet` is unchanged.\n107:Add `QUIET=false` beside `JSON_OUTPUT`, accept `--quiet` in the parser, and exit 1 with a stderr message when `--json` is also set.\n109:Acceptance: `--quiet` is accepted, `--json --quiet` exits 1, and no scoring function reads `QUIET`.\n111:Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --quiet --json --loc 50 --files 2 >/dev/null 2>&1; echo $?` prints `1`.\n115:Print only the level line when `QUIET` is true, then add the option to the header block and `show_help`.\n117:Acceptance: quiet prints exactly one line, the default report is unchanged, and both help surfaces list the flag.\n119:Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural | wc -l` prints `1`.\n129:| Unit | Argument parsing and the quiet branch: accepted flag, rejected `--json` pair, single output line | `bash -n`, direct invocation, `wc -l` |\n130:| Integration | Default, quiet and JSON modes across low, medium and full-risk inputs, plus the error paths | Captured stdout and stderr, `diff`, exit codes |\n152:- **Trigger**: The default report changes, or `--quiet` alters an exit code or a stderr message.\n210:| Parser change | Baseline capture | Accepted `--quiet`, rejected `--json` pair | Quiet branch |\n221:2. **Add the parser and the quiet branch** - 25 minutes - CRITICAL\n227:- The header and `show_help` documentation runs alongside the quiet branch, since both edit the same file but different regions.\n239:| M2 | Flag works | `--quiet` prints one line and `--json --quiet` exits `1` | Phase 2 |\n253:**Decision**: Add `--quiet` to the existing argument parser and store it in a `QUIET` global beside `JSON_OUTPUT`.\n260:- `SPEC_RECOMMEND_QUIET` environment variable: invisible in `--help`, inherited by child processes, and easy to leave set by accident.\n263:### ADR-002: Reject `--quiet --json` instead of picking a winner\n267:**Context**: `--quiet` asks for one text line and `--json` asks for a JSON document. A caller that passes both has made a mistake, and either silent resolution hides it.\n273:- A caller that wants the level from JSON keeps using `--json` and reads `recommended_level`; a caller that wants one line uses `--quiet`.\n276:- Let `--quiet` win: silently drops the JSON contract the caller asked for.\n277:- Let `--json` win: silently ignores the flag, so the caller believes the output is quiet.\n284:**Context**: `output_text` already prints `Recommended Level: N (Name)`. A quiet mode that invents a new format gives callers a second contract to track.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"0bfdfd","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_2f41cfc5f083480898538871d5c40b47","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"  # Each risk factor adds some confidence (shows thoroughness)\n  bonus=$((bonus + risk_factors * 2))\n\n  # If score is near threshold boundaries, reduce confidence\n  local distance_to_boundary=100\n  local boundaries=(\"$LEVEL_0_MAX\" \"$LEVEL_1_MAX\" \"$LEVEL_2_MAX\")\n  for boundary in \"${boundaries[@]}\"; do\n    local diff=$((TOTAL_SCORE - boundary))\n    if [[ \"$diff\" -lt 0 ]]; then diff=$((-diff)); fi\n    if [[ \"$diff\" -lt \"$distance_to_boundary\" ]]; then\n      distance_to_boundary=$diff\n    fi\n  done\n\n  # Reduce confidence if very close to a boundary (within 5 points)\n  if [[ \"$distance_to_boundary\" -le 5 ]]; then\n    bonus=$((bonus - 10))\n  fi\n\n  CONFIDENCE=$((base_confidence + bonus))\n\n  # Cap at 95% (never 100% certain)\n  if [[ \"$CONFIDENCE\" -gt 95 ]]; then\n    CONFIDENCE=95\n  fi\n\n  # Minimum 50%\n  if [[ \"$CONFIDENCE\" -lt 50 ]]; then\n    CONFIDENCE=50\n  fi\n}\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 4. OUTPUT FUNCTIONS\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Output_text()\n# Output results in human-readable text format\noutput_text() {\n  echo \"\"\n  echo \"Recommended Level: ${RECOMMENDED_LEVEL} (${LEVEL_NAME})\"\n  echo \"Score: ${TOTAL_SCORE}/100 | Confidence: ${CONFIDENCE}%\"\n  echo \"\"\n  echo \"Breakdown:\"\n  echo \"- LOC (${LOC}): +${SCORE_LOC} points\"\n  echo \"- Files (${FILES}): +${SCORE_FILES} points\"\n  echo -n \"- API changes: \"\n  if [[ \"$HAS_API\" = true ]]; then\n    echo \"+${POINTS_API} points\"\n  else\n    echo \"+0 points\"\n  fi\n  echo -n \"- Auth changes: \"\n  if [[ \"$HAS_AUTH\" = true ]]; then\n    echo \"+${POINTS_AUTH} points\"\n  else\n    echo \"+0 points\"\n  fi\n  echo -n \"- DB changes: \"\n  if [[ \"$HAS_DB\" = true ]]; then\n    echo \"+${POINTS_DB} points\"\n# Determine recommended level\ndetermine_level \"$TOTAL_SCORE\"\n\n# Calculate confidence\ncalculate_confidence\n\n# Calculate phase recommendation (default on; opt-out via --no-recommend-phases)\nif [[ \"$RECOMMEND_PHASES\" = true ]]; then\n  determine_phasing\nfi\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 7. OUTPUT RESULTS\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nif [[ \"$JSON_OUTPUT\" = true ]]; then\n  output_json\nelse\n  output_text\nfi\n\nexit 0\n\n# Exit codes:\n#   0 - Success\n#   1 - ERROR: --loc requires a numeric value\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"6a9274","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
